  "id": "perceptual-defense",
  "term": "Perceptual Defense",
  "definition": "Perceptual defense is a selective form of perception in which a person protects themselves from becoming aware of something unpleasant or threatening. Because of this, threatening words may be misheard or violent actions may be perceived less accurately.",
